(55530, 1294, 1078, '<td valign="top">I would have scored this one higher -- I think the idea has possibility -- but the clouds are so blown out -- it''s almost as if you have blue clouds in a white sky -- did you have to play with the levels or the camera''s metering to get the wall to show up at the expense of an overly bright sky?  Maybe shooting at another time of day when the son could either create highlights and shadows on the wall -- or at least make the sky a little less bright...</td>', 'I would have scored this one higher -- I think the idea has possibility -- but the clouds are so blown out -- it''s almost as if you have blue clouds in a white sky -- did you have to play with the levels or the camera''s metering to get the wall to show up at the expense of an overly bright sky?  Maybe shooting at another time of day when the son could either create highlights and shadows on the wall -- or at least make the sky a little less bright...', '2002-04-30 12:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(55531, 1294, 888, '<td valign="top">nice rugged wall but with no clue as to what it is it loses something.  I think the skys a little over exposed too</td>', 'nice rugged wall but with no clue as to what it is it loses something.  I think the skys a little over exposed too', '2002-04-30 13:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(55532, 1294, 1041, '<td valign="top">Nice angle!  Like the wall.  Good focus.  Was there anything on the wall that could''ve held the eyes interest a little more?  A bug, or bird, or plant growing through a crack?  Also, the sky seems a little overexposed.</td>', 'Nice angle!  Like the wall.  Good focus.  Was there anything on the wall that could''ve held the eyes interest a little more?  A bug, or bird, or plant growing through a crack?  Also, the sky seems a little overexposed.', '2002-05-01 10:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(55533, 1294, 543, '<td valign="top">A very tough lighting situation - open shade and hot sky.  WIth a digital camera, it''s better to expose for the highlights and then retrieve the shadow detail later in software - just the opposite of film.  Good detail in the wal.</td>', 'A very tough lighting situation - open shade and hot sky.  WIth a digital camera, it''s better to expose for the highlights and then retrieve the shadow detail later in software - just the opposite of film.  Good detail in the wal.', '2002-05-01 11:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
