(56219, 1328, 1070, '<td valign="top">First Impressions- would have liked to have seen this image symmetrical, or even in colour.  BUT You''ve achieved a more intersting shot with the black and white giving it a gothic feel.</td>', 'First Impressions- would have liked to have seen this image symmetrical, or even in colour.  BUT You''ve achieved a more intersting shot with the black and white giving it a gothic feel.', '2002-05-05 11:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56220, 1328, 749, '<td valign="top">I love the contrast between the textures of the masonry and the glass - very nice!</td>', 'I love the contrast between the textures of the masonry and the glass - very nice!', '2002-05-05 14:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56221, 1328, 1, '<td valign="top">A better centering job would''ve been more dramatic.</td>', 'A better centering job would''ve been more dramatic.', '2002-05-05 22:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56222, 1328, 772, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments on this photo... I chose to do this photo in black and white because the concrete molding in and around the window had a rather ugly green tint due to the lighting and the trees.  I ruined this photo by naming it ''Stained Class'' which indicates the presence of color... I should have chosen a more appropriate name...</td>', 'Thanks for the comments on this photo... I chose to do this photo in black and white because the concrete molding in and around the window had a rather ugly green tint due to the lighting and the trees.  I ruined this photo by naming it ''Stained Class'' which indicates the presence of color... I should have chosen a more appropriate name...', '2002-05-06 21:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(56223, 1329, 772, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting statue photograph.  I like the angle of this shot too.  The only issue I have with this shot is that the ''belly'' area of this statue has, what I like to call, a ''hot spot''.  This is an area where the light is a little too bright on the photo.  I believe your flash may have caused this.  When this happens, you can either try to set your flash to a lower power mode or you can veil the flash with something like a piece of sheer cloth material or something to reduce and disperse the light away from the subject just a little.  Sometimes, scotch tape can be used to achieve this...</td>', 'This is an interesting statue photograph.  I like the angle of this shot too.  The only issue I have with this shot is that the ''belly'' area of this statue has, what I like to call, a ''hot spot''.  This is an area where the light is a little too bright on the photo.  I believe your flash may have caused this.  When this happens, you can either try to set your flash to a lower power mode or you can veil the flash with something like a piece of sheer cloth material or something to reduce and disperse the light away from the subject just a little.  Sometimes, scotch tape can be used to achieve this...', '2002-04-29 08:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56224, 1329, 656, '<td valign="top">flash seems to have washed this out</td>', 'flash seems to have washed this out', '2002-04-29 10:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56225, 1329, 259, '<td valign="top">the flash is a little harsh.</td>', 'the flash is a little harsh.', '2002-04-29 10:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56226, 1329, 280, '<td valign="top">I think there is too much light on the front of the statue.</td>', 'I think there is too much light on the front of the statue.', '2002-04-29 11:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56227, 1329, 1175, '<td valign="top">That''s a nice picture.  Was it at night and were you using your flash?  That''s what it looks like.  A change in lighting is necessary, that or turn the flash off and open your aperture all the way and slow the shutter speed to let the light in.</td>', 'That''s a nice picture.  Was it at night and were you using your flash?  That''s what it looks like.  A change in lighting is necessary, that or turn the flash off and open your aperture all the way and slow the shutter speed to let the light in.', '2002-04-29 12:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(56228, 1329, 1336, '<td valign="top">not lit very well</td>', 'not lit very well', '2002-04-29 14:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
